diff --git a/specs/hal-engine-tool-input-validation/spec.md b/specs/hal-engine-tool-input-validation/spec.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..db7ead1
--- /dev/null
+++ b/specs/hal-engine-tool-input-validation/spec.md
@@ -0,0 +1,37 @@
+# Tool Input Validation
+
+| Field  | Value                |
+| ------ | -------------------- |
+| Issue  | re-cinq/HALEngine#37 |
+| Status | In Progress          |
+
+Every tool registered in `src/orchestration/tools/registry.ts` declares a JSON Schema `inputSchema` that is forwarded to the configured AI provider, and `ToolRegistry.execute` validates the model-supplied `input` against that schema before calling the tool's executor. When validation fails, `execute` returns a rejection `ToolResponse` describing what was wrong rather than throwing, so the orchestrator feeds the failure back to the model as a `tool_result` within the existing tool-round budget.
+
+## Validation at execute time
+
+- A missing required property is rejected before the executor runs, and the returned result identifies that property as required ([validated by: rejects input missing a required property and never calls the executor](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.test.ts#L22)).
+- When `input` omits a property listed in `required`, `ToolRegistry.execute` returns a `ToolResponse` whose `result` names the missing property as required and never invokes the executor ([validated by: rejects input missing a required property with a ToolResponse and never calls the executor](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L16)).
+- When `input` supplies a property whose value does not match its declared JSON Schema type, `ToolRegistry.execute` returns a `ToolResponse` naming the failing field path and expected type without invoking the executor, and neither `result` nor the emitted log record contains the offending property value ([validated by: rejects a wrong-typed property with its field path and expected type without exposing its value](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.test.ts#L35); [validated by: rejects a wrong-typed property naming the field and expected type without leaking the offending value to the result or logs](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L46)).
+- A nested wrong-typed property is reported with its complete field path ([validated by: reports a nested invalid property path](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.test.ts#L50)).
+- A root property with the wrong type is reported by its field name and expected type ([validated by: names a root property when its value has the wrong type](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.test.ts#L69); [validated by: reports the root property path from a type validation error](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.test.ts#L105)).
+- A property value outside its declared `enum` is rejected before the executor runs, and the result identifies the property and enum constraint ([validated by: rejects a property value outside its declared enum](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.test.ts#L78)).
+- When a schema explicitly disallows an extra property, the rejection identifies that property and the `additionalProperties` constraint without exposing its value ([validated by: reports a disallowed property path without exposing its value](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.test.ts#L114)).
+- When `input` satisfies `required`, declared property types and `enum`, `ToolRegistry.execute` invokes the executor once and passes the input object through unchanged — including undeclared extra properties — without injecting `additionalProperties: false`, coercing types or applying defaults ([validated by: passes valid input with undeclared properties through unchanged exactly once](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.test.ts#L137)).
+- When a tool call fails input validation, the orchestrator passes the rejection result to the provider on the next round, where the model can retry with corrected input ([validated by returns a schema rejection to the provider before a corrected retry](../../src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.test.ts#L401)); it forwards client messages returned by a tool in the same `tool_result` chunk ([validated by: forwards the client messages a tool returned as one tool_result chunk](../../src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.test.ts#L481)).
+- When `ToolRegistry.execute` is called with a tool name that has not been registered, it throws `Unknown tool: <name>` because an unregistered tool is a programming or configuration error rather than a recoverable input mistake ([validated by: throws for an unregistered tool name](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.test.ts#L131)).
+
+## Schema compilation and caching
+
+- A static `ToolDefinition` has its `inputSchema` compiled once at `register` time, so a schema that is not valid JSON Schema throws synchronously from `register` with an error message naming the offending tool ([validated by throws at registration naming the tool when its static schema is invalid](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.test.ts#L176); [validated by throws at register time naming the tool when a static inputSchema cannot be compiled](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L94)).
+- A static tool's `inputSchema` is compiled at `register` time and reused on every `execute` call without re-reading or re-compiling `definition.inputSchema` ([validated by: compiles a static schema once across repeated executions](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.test.ts#L190)).
+- A function-valued `ToolDefinitionSource` resolves its definition on each `execute` call and validates against the `inputSchema` returned for that call, caching compiled validators by schema object reference (`WeakMap`) so distinct returned schemas each enforce their own rules.
+- The function-valued definition's current schema is used on each call, even when a previous call returned a different schema ([validated by: validates function-valued definitions against the schema returned for each call](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.test.ts#L153)).
+- The orchestrator stops after one model response when no tool call is requested ([validated by: stops after one round when nothing asked for a tool](../../src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.test.ts#L458)).
+- A tool can request that the orchestrator suppress the assistant response ([validated by: asks for suppression when the tool says the reply is already handled](../../src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.test.ts#L511)).
+- Text reported across rounds is joined before the response hook receives it ([validated by: joins the text of every round, not only the last](../../src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.test.ts#L523)).
+- Usage reported in an earlier round is retained when a later round omits usage ([validated by: keeps the usage an earlier round reported when a later round reports none](../../src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.test.ts#L545)).
+
+## Orchestrator tool-loop recovery
+
+- Because a schema rejection returns a `ToolResponse` instead of throwing, `src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.ts` sends the rejection `result` back to the provider as a `tool_result` message, allowing the model to issue a corrected tool call on the next round and complete the turn within `maxToolRounds` ([validated by: returns a schema rejection as a tool_result in the orchestrator loop so the model can correct the call on the next round](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L112)).
+- Valid input retains undeclared properties and reaches the executor unchanged exactly once ([validated by: passes valid input with undeclared properties through unchanged exactly once](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.test.ts#L120)).
